    "updated_at": "2025-10-31T17:46:03Z",
    "body": "> Not sure. It seems [if you call `<option>.selected` earlier, you get a slightly different result](https://software.hixie.ch/utilities/js/live-dom-viewer/?%3Cselect%20id%3Dselect%3E%0A%20%20%3Coption%20id%3Done%3Eone%3C%2Foption%3E%0A%20%20%3Coption%20id%3Dtwo%3Etwo%3C%2Foption%3E%0A%3C%2Fselect%3E%0A%3Cscript%3E%0Aone%20%3D%20document.getElementById(%27one%27)%3B%0Atwo%20%3D%20document.getElementById(%27two%27)%3B%0Aw(one.selected)%3B%0Aw(two.selected)%3B%0Aselect.innerHTML%20%3D%20%27%27%3B%0Aw(one.selected)%3B%0Aw(two.selected)%3B%0Aselect.appendChild(one)%3B%0Aselect.appendChild(two)%3B%0Aw(select.value)%3B%0A%3C%2Fscript%3E). That it differs depending on observation seems like a bug.\n\nI see, that is odd. I wonder what's going on.\n\n\n\n> The problem is that when we run the insertion callback for _option3_, we mark that as the selected option and therefore _option4_ gets deselected because it's already in the tree at that point. And you can't fix this by having insertion behavior for `optgroup` elements, because when that callback runs, the callback for the `option` elements hasn't run yet and they won't have a `select` element owner yet.\n\nIn chromium, each option will have its insertion steps called twice: once when they are inserted into the optgroup, and a second time when the optgroup is appended to the select element.\n\nDuring the first insertion into the optgroup, the selectedness of each option should remain true due to the defaultSelected.\n\nDuring the second insertion, option 3 runs its insertion steps and then option 4 runs its insertion steps. It would make sense that option 3 deselects the other options during its insertion (via the selectedness setting algorithm) and therefore makes option 4 not get selected, but it looks like we have [some code which prevents that from happening](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/blink/renderer/core/html/forms/html_select_element.cc;l=1050-1052;drc=45a1118875a1b3a2a1ae9fee639cf1b546a43547): since option 4 hasn't had its insertion steps run yet which assigned a [cached nearest ancestor select](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#cached-nearest-ancestor-select-element), it doesn't get deselected.\n\nWe could modify the selectedness setting algorithm to run like this by checking each option's cached nearest ancestor select.\n\nDoes this make sense? Does that sound like a good spec change?",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
